                "entry_id": "7059fa4e-e2c4-306e-9ee3-6509b2fb0eef",
                "word": "cathéter",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2c423d56-a3c7-4a93-be1b-cbfdb84b4622",
                        "entry_id": "7059fa4e-e2c4-306e-9ee3-6509b2fb0eef",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "cathéters"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "db6a970e-8f4c-315c-8945-3aefb8cd3832",
                        "entry_id": "7059fa4e-e2c4-306e-9ee3-6509b2fb0eef",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Instrument médical consistant en un tuyau souple et fin (moins d'un millimètre d'épaisseur), qui est destiné à être placé relativement longtemps dans une veine, pour réaliser des injections ou perfusions prolongées ou répétées. Il améliore le confort du patient en évitant de le piquer à plusieurs reprises."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "55e55fd1-8c64-40a9-99af-27dd66957446",
                                "sense_id": "db6a970e-8f4c-315c-8945-3aefb8cd3832",
                                "text": "Lucile avait arrêté de fumer, son avenir s’énonçait en termes de cures, de cycles, de rayons, de cathéter, elle essaya néanmoins de parler d’autre chose, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ba5dc521-6fa2-41c7-9063-875bdd078e7a",
                                "sense_id": "db6a970e-8f4c-315c-8945-3aefb8cd3832",
                                "text": "En moins de temps qu’il ne faut pour le dire, le médecin se pencha sur l’enfant et planta un cathéter dans sa trachée, juste en dessous de la pomme d’Adam."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2dfc04d3-6277-4144-a5cc-b6b9abd27070",
                        "source_entry_id": "7059fa4e-e2c4-306e-9ee3-6509b2fb0eef",
                        "source_sense_id": "db6a970e-8f4c-315c-8945-3aefb8cd3832",
                        "target_lang_word": "Katheter",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Katheter",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "78998305-9a50-318c-a576-14e632a87d89",
                                        "entry_id": "6cd97ae3-048e-3d21-9239-1cf8c76ed4d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Röhrchen oder Schlauch aus Kunststoff, Latex, Silikon, Metall oder Glas, mit denen Hohlorgane wie Harnblase, Magen, Darm, Gefäße und so weiter, aber auch Ohr und Herz sondiert, entleert, gefüllt oder gespült werden können"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c45acd58-5257-4f41-9518-595bcff7ce8b",
                                                "sense_id": "78998305-9a50-318c-a576-14e632a87d89",
                                                "text": "Wenn jemand nicht urinieren kann, muss oft ein Katheter gelegt werden."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e562e356-b858-4ffd-b57d-678479d0aa4d",
                                                "sense_id": "78998305-9a50-318c-a576-14e632a87d89",
                                                "text": "„Ein anderer Statist musste die ganze Zeit auf einer Tragbahre mit dem Katheter in der Hand liegen und laut stöhnen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e06eb68-322c-4689-a3db-e882c10bfa6f",
                                                "sense_id": "78998305-9a50-318c-a576-14e632a87d89",
                                                "text": "„Sie nahm meinen Unterarm, suchte und fand eine Vene und stach mir eine Nadel hinein, legte einen Katheter.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d8bd7f00-5146-4b1b-8ac4-ba10bc5c988c",
                        "source_entry_id": "7059fa4e-e2c4-306e-9ee3-6509b2fb0eef",
                        "source_sense_id": "db6a970e-8f4c-315c-8945-3aefb8cd3832",
                        "target_lang_word": "catheter",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "catheter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2d4f071d-96bc-3348-888f-cb9cf19200d2",
                                        "entry_id": "390b7a6e-debc-3add-a305-cecb6af4cc95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small tube inserted into a body cavity to administer a drug, create an opening, distend a passageway, or remove fluid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae5d3171-ddf0-4d5c-a210-efff45796d6e",
                                                "sense_id": "2d4f071d-96bc-3348-888f-cb9cf19200d2",
                                                "text": "And I humbly hope, that the Deſcription, and the Method of uſing this Catheter, will be a means of reviving an Operation ſo happily begun, and calculated for the Good of thoſe that are afflicted with the Stone in the Bladder."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17ac5f16-cf51-44bd-ac96-1682691a185f",
                                                "sense_id": "2d4f071d-96bc-3348-888f-cb9cf19200d2",
                                                "text": "Of course there are two kinds of catheters, one intended for the male, the other for the female urethra. The common catheter is a silver tube, of such diameter as will allow it to be introduced with ease into the urethra, and of various figures and lengths, according as it is intended for the young or adult, the male or female, subject."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c577fada-f946-4cb9-8cc4-996ebf651853",
                                                "sense_id": "2d4f071d-96bc-3348-888f-cb9cf19200d2",
                                                "text": "Careful positioning of the catheter is essential to achieve a technically satisfactory dialysis. Final placement is made by assessing drainage and by positioning the tip of the catheter according to the patient's comfort."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c0f85e5-80eb-4d53-a5ad-46ccfe04edca",
                                                "sense_id": "2d4f071d-96bc-3348-888f-cb9cf19200d2",
                                                "text": "Embryos are transferred into a womb using a long, soft catheter attached to a syringe containing the embryos in a transfer solution. The catheter is threaded through the endocervical canal (\"birth canal\") into the uterine cavity under ultrasound guidance, and the embryos are deposited gently high in the womb."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f48d8615-467f-4096-89f4-ac64b15257b0",
